course: dictionary
lesson: 13841
title: The jeweller
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A jeweller is a person who makes, sells or repairs jewellery and watches. Jewellery means things you wear, like rings, necklaces and bracelets. «Mum took her broken necklace to the jeweller.» The necklace is broken, so the jeweller must be someone who can fix it.
explain: The word can also mean a shop. «We walked past the jeweller's and stopped to look at the sparkling rings in the window.» The apostrophe s shows the shop belongs to the jeweller. Clues like window and sparkling rings tell you it is a shop, not a person.
explain: When you meet a new word, read the words around it. Ask: what would fit here? A jeweller can mend a clasp, but a baker cannot. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A jeweller is a person who makes, sells or repairs jewellery and watches.
fact: A jeweller's is a shop that sells jewellery.
fact: Jewellery means things you wear, such as rings, necklaces and bracelets.
fact: The plural is jewellers, as in «There are two jewellers on our street.»
fact: In the US the word is spelled jeweler, with one l in the middle.
exercise: «The jeweller fixed the clasp on Mum's gold necklace.» What is a jeweller? | A shop that sells only shoes | A person who drives a bus | *A person who makes, sells or repairs jewellery and watches
exercise: «We went to the jeweller's to buy a birthday ring.» Find and copy the word that shows a shop. | *jeweller's | went | ring | birthday
exercise: Which spelling is the British one used in this lesson? | *jeweller | jewelr | jeweler | jewelery
test: «The jeweller showed us a ring with a tiny blue stone.» What does the jeweller do? | Teaches music | *Makes and sells jewellery | Drives the bus | Grows flowers in a garden
test: «Dad took his old watch to the jeweller to get the glass mended.» What did the jeweller probably do to the watch? | Read it aloud | Posted it to the moon | Fed it to the birds | *Repaired it
exam: «Maya saved for months to buy a bracelet from the jeweller's on Market Street.» What is the jeweller's? | A school for artists | A park with swings | A kind of bird | *A shop that sells jewellery
